From 6716fad19583a9a8cfafe45826058a8e2754ef3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:57:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(pick): box-select edge chains and faces into an
 operation's picks

Ctrl (or Shift) + left drag in the viewport, in Edge or Face mode with an
operation open, draws a rubber band instead of orbiting. Its release adds
every visible feature edge chain (Edge mode) or welded face (Face mode)
in the box to the operation's picks as one SetOperationGeometry - one
undo step. A drag to the right is a window (wholly inside), to the left
a crossing box (inside or touching). The #692 one pick rule holds:
feature chains only, and a candidate counts only if part of it is
unoccluded from the eye (the click pick's own sight test); stock and
fixtures are never candidates but still occlude.

The rule is app::pick::box_pick (box_bodies / box_select /
box_select_top); the gesture is ui::box_pick. MCP twin: pick_in_box, a
world X/Y box seen from straight above.

Decisions: docs/decisions/979-box-select-picks.md.

Fixes #979

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
